Adventure 2: The Long Road West
Campaign: Ismara's Doom — The Parks Group
 Tier: Apprentice (2 AP -> 3 AP)
 Players: 4-6
 Estimated Play Time: 2-3 Sessions
 Reward: 1 Advancement Point
 New Companion: Caelan the Fox, recruited at the Atmoran Scholar's Ruin,
 on the road to Solitude (see `Ismara's-doom/npcs/caelan the fox (early
 state)`)
 Companion Documents: `Ismara's-doom/cities/solitude`, `Ismara's-doom/
 cities/morthal`, `Ismara's-doom/cities/dawnstar` — city profiles
 (services, shops, background NPCs, downtime event tables) for the three
 holds this adventure touches. For prep and downtime reference; none
 needed mid-scene.

Adventure Summary
Bjorn's own trade circuit takes the party west out of Windhelm — the
Pale, then Morthal, then Solitude, before the mountain passes shut for
the season. Ismara's single-word note, "West," rides on top of a reason
that was never about her. She needs nodes across three holds. The party
is about to watch that happen in the open, at a scale they can no
longer mistake for background noise.
The Pale Fever pattern from Windhelm repeats on the road: frozen
people, standing, alive, eyes tracking. In Morthal it reads as
something else entirely — a vampire coven's slow predation, which looks
like Ismara's work and isn't, already ended by someone else entirely.
On the road to Solitude, Caelan the Fox joins them at a locked door. In
Solitude, Ismara makes her most direct persuasion move yet, and a man
who runs the city's shadows quietly notices something about her that
should worry everyone. In a village outside the city, Ismara makes her
first demand with real moral weight: two people, or she chooses
herself. The truth they still don't have: what happens to the nodes
when the ritual completes. That doesn't arrive until Riften, Adventure
4.

